# Network Requests

Network requests are handled with the `JumpNetworkService` in `jump_connect` library. 
- This provides a custom network request called `JumpNetworkRequest` which takes two generic types T and K.
- K is the actual type we decode into, i.e. OrderDto.
- T is either just K if api returns a single object, else it is `List<K>` if api returns multiple
- All network calls should be made inside datasources or infra services
- We provide an authenticated network service client or an unauthenticated one, all bff calls except auth require authenticated and all external calls should use unauthenticated